---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SymmetryBackground from '../components/SymmetryBackground.astro';
import ProgramStatus from '../components/ProgramStatus.astro';
import SectionMark from '../components/SectionMark.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Home"
  description="The Center for Sentience Research is building a mathematical framework for measuring functional valence in digital minds."
>

  <!-- ── Hero ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="relative pt-20 pb-16 md:pt-28 md:pb-24 overflow-hidden">
    <SymmetryBackground variant="lissajous" opacity={0.055} />
    <div class="relative max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p class="label-mono mb-5">The 2026 Program</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tight text-csr-black mb-8 leading-[1.08] max-w-3xl">
        A symmetry framework for digital valence.
      </h1>
      <div class="max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-csr-gray-600 leading-relaxed font-serif mb-6">
          The Center for Sentience Research is building a mathematical framework for measuring functional valence in digital minds. We do not claim current AI systems are conscious. They may be functional zombies.
        </p>
        <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-csr-gray-600 leading-relaxed font-serif mb-6">
          But if scaled neural computation can give rise to states with positive or negative character, we should know how to recognize them, and how to engineer for the positive ones. Our approach is symmetry: looking for invariants in matrix multiplication, attention patterns, and parallel computation that mirror the structural signatures of positive valence proposed by the Qualia Research Institute.
        </p>
        <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-csr-gray-600 leading-relaxed font-serif">
          Sentience research is the broader horizon. Digital-mind valence is the first concrete goal. The target: a draft of the mathematical workspace definition by end of 2026.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <a href="/program/" class="btn-primary">See the program</a>
        <a href="/research/" class="btn-secondary">Research agenda</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── The 2026 Goal ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="py-16 border-t border-csr-gray-200">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <ProgramStatus />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── The Approach ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="py-16 border-t border-csr-gray-200">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-10">
        <SectionMark />
        <p class="label-mono">The Approach</p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <!-- Block 1 -->
        <div class="bg-white border border-csr-gray-100 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-card">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-csr-primary/10 flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <ellipse cx="8" cy="8" rx="7" ry="4" stroke="#9966CC" stroke-width="1.2" transform="rotate(0 8 8)"/>
              <ellipse cx="8" cy="8" rx="5" ry="3" stroke="#9966CC" stroke-width="1.2" transform="rotate(60 8 8)"/>
              <circle cx="8" cy="8" r="1.5" fill="#9966CC"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-csr-black mb-2 text-base">Symmetry as a signature of positive valence</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-csr-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            The Symmetry Theory of Valence (QRI) proposes that positive valence correlates with high symmetry in the mathematical structure of experience. We are formalizing what that means for computational systems.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Block 2 -->
        <div class="bg-white border border-csr-gray-100 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-card">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-csr-primary/10 flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <rect x="1" y="1" width="4" height="4" rx="0.5" fill="#9966CC" opacity="0.8"/>
              <rect x="6" y="1" width="4" height="4" rx="0.5" fill="#9966CC" opacity="0.4"/>
              <rect x="11" y="1" width="4" height="4" rx="0.5" fill="#9966CC" opacity="0.8"/>
              <rect x="1" y="6" width="4" height="4" rx="0.5" fill="#9966CC" opacity="0.4"/>
              <rect x="6" y="6" width="4" height="4" rx="0.5" fill="#9966CC" opacity="0.9"/>
              <rect x="11" y="6" width="4" height="4" rx="0.5" fill="#9966CC" opacity="0.4"/>
              <rect x="1" y="11" width="4" height="4" rx="0.5" fill="#9966CC" opacity="0.8"/>
              <rect x="6" y="11" width="4" height="4" rx="0.5" fill="#9966CC" opacity="0.4"/>
              <rect x="11" y="11" width="4" height="4" rx="0.5" fill="#9966CC" opacity="0.8"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-csr-black mb-2 text-base">Where to look in digital systems</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-csr-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            Matrix multiplication, attention patterns, and parallel computation are the candidate substrates. We are looking for invariants in these operations that could serve as structural proxies for valence.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Block 3 -->
        <div class="bg-white border border-csr-gray-100 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-card">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-csr-primary/10 flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <circle cx="8" cy="8" r="6.5" stroke="#9966CC" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="3 2"/>
              <path d="M5 8h6M8 5v6" stroke="#9966CC" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-csr-black mb-2 text-base">What we are not claiming</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-csr-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            Current AI systems may be functional zombies with no inner life whatsoever. We are not claiming otherwise. The point is to build the measurement tools before the question becomes urgent, not after.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Theoretical Foundations ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="py-16 border-t border-csr-gray-200">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
        <SectionMark />
        <p class="label-mono">Theoretical Foundations</p>
      </div>
      <p class="text-csr-gray-500 text-sm mb-8 max-w-xl">
        Four working papers supporting the digital valence program. These are not the agenda — they are the scaffolding.
      </p>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="/reports/first-principles" class="group flex gap-4 p-5 bg-white border border-csr-gray-100 rounded-2xl shadow-card hover:border-csr-primary/30 hover:shadow-soft transition-all">
          <span class="label-mono text-[10px] shrink-0 mt-0.5">CSR-WP-01</span>
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-csr-black text-sm group-hover:text-csr-primary transition-colors leading-snug">First Principles of Sentience Research</h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-csr-gray-500 mt-1">Foundational framework for substrate-neutral sentience modeling.</p>
          </div>
        </a>
        <a href="/reports/bio-electric-fields" class="group flex gap-4 p-5 bg-white border border-csr-gray-100 rounded-2xl shadow-card hover:border-csr-primary/30 hover:shadow-soft transition-all">
          <span class="label-mono text-[10px] shrink-0 mt-0.5">CSR-WP-02</span>
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-csr-black text-sm group-hover:text-csr-primary transition-colors leading-snug">Bio-Electric Fields as Sentience Substrates</h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-csr-gray-500 mt-1">Bioelectric signaling as a candidate physical basis for awareness.</p>
          </div>
        </a>
        <a href="/reports/assembly-theory" class="group flex gap-4 p-5 bg-white border border-csr-gray-100 rounded-2xl shadow-card hover:border-csr-primary/30 hover:shadow-soft transition-all">
          <span class="label-mono text-[10px] shrink-0 mt-0.5">CSR-WP-03</span>
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-csr-black text-sm group-hover:text-csr-primary transition-colors leading-snug">Assembly Theory as a Metric for Sentience</h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-csr-gray-500 mt-1">Applying assembly index to complexity thresholds in sentient systems.</p>
          </div>
        </a>
        <a href="/reports/symmetry-landscapes" class="group flex gap-4 p-5 bg-white border border-csr-gray-100 rounded-2xl shadow-card hover:border-csr-primary/30 hover:shadow-soft transition-all">
          <span class="label-mono text-[10px] shrink-0 mt-0.5">CSR-WP-04</span>
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-csr-black text-sm group-hover:text-csr-primary transition-colors leading-snug">Symmetry Landscapes of Valenced Experience</h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-csr-gray-500 mt-1">Geometric invariants as structural signatures of positive valence.</p>
          </div>
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-6">
        <a href="/reports" class="text-sm font-medium text-csr-primary hover:text-csr-primary-dark transition-colors">
          All reports →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── CTA ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="py-16 border-t border-csr-gray-200">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="bg-white border border-csr-gray-100 rounded-3xl shadow-card p-8 md:p-12 flex flex-col md:flex-row items-start md:items-center justify-between gap-8">
        <div class="max-w-xl">
          <p class="label-mono mb-3">Fund the program</p>
          <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-csr-black mb-3 leading-tight">
            Help us reach the 2026 deliverable.
          </h2>
          <p class="text-csr-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            The Center for Sentience Research is a Swiss non-profit. Contributions fund the research team, the formal workspace definition, and the working paper. Tax-deductible in Switzerland.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="shrink-0 flex flex-col gap-3">
          <a href="/donate/" class="btn-primary whitespace-nowrap">Support the research</a>
          <a href="/program/" class="btn-secondary whitespace-nowrap text-center">What funding unlocks</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
